      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BRONNY'S BLUE (8) hit the ground running and was prominent to the turn but faded out of it when 7th at Gosford in Grade 5 company. Safe beginner but wide box to overcome and will need some luck. Has ability and can bounce back. BEEF KEBAB (2) filled the minor money two on end before breaking through for a deserved win last time, scoring at this track over 320m (18.53). Smart beginner who should take advantage of the low draw. Likely to be in the finish. REBORN JESTER (1) has missed the frame the last couple but was a Maiden winner three back (18.57) at this track over 320m. With a good start should be able to take advantage of the rails draw. Expecting significant improvement. SPRING CRUISER (7) in the money here last time and looks a top-three prospect again.",
